  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A plane electromagnetic wave of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MHz</mi></math> is traveling in a vacuum along the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo></math>direction. At a particular point in space and time, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. The value of the electric field at this point is:(speed of light <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> are unit vectors along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;direction.</p>"
